From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_MIB=N holds N MiB of the pool for the driver's own small buffers

T185a. At the load past Ocarina's field the pool is at its last MiB for
seconds in every start (the cold-start test at the field on T184; RADV_PS5_MEMORY
available_mib 0-2). The app survives a refused image or buffer, but not a
refused descriptor pool (vkCreateDescriptorPool from a draw on the Vulkan
worker: run1430 T177, run1473 T184) or a refused upload buffer
(radv_cmd_buffer_resize_upload_buf records VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY as
the command buffer's error and vkEndCommandBuffer returns it: run1455, run1475).
Both carry RADEON_FLAG_32BIT, so radv_ps5_memory_alloc returns before
lead-mesh-22's eden_radv_out_of_memory for them (and for the app's buffers,
which do ask, Eden gave back 0 MiB in every logged call at this load).

A limit on the app's allocations alone (refuse VkDeviceMemory while the pool
has N MiB or less) would not keep the last MiB for the driver: the guest's
memory, the JIT and the heap draw on the same pool (the heap grew 64-146 MiB in
those 2 s). So the driver holds the memory: N MiB as separate 2 MiB blocks of
direct memory, allocated and not mapped. When the pool refuses a buffer of
priority above RADV_BO_PRIORITY_APPLICATION_MAX (not VkDeviceMemory), not
replayable and of 2 MiB or less, after the retired-memory wait, one block goes
back to the kernel and the buffer is placed again by the same
radv_ps5_memory_alloc_once (at most two blocks per buffer; a block whose retry
fails went to another thread and counts as lost). The served buffer is an
ordinary allocation: freeing and retiring are unchanged. The reserve is filled
at the first buffer and again, at most every 250 ms, once the largest free
piece is N + RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_REFILL_MIB (default 256) MiB or more.
The app's device memory sees a pool N MiB smaller the whole time.

Not served: the 8 MiB shader arenas, the 64 MiB gs heap, scratch and rings
(over 2 MiB), the submission ring's dedicated buffers for very long streams
(radv_ps5_queue_claim, not a buffer), and the host's own memory (command
stream chunks are malloc'd: their failure is VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY).

Lines (stderr), at the fill, at each of the first 48 events and every 64th:
  RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE on: filled|refilled|served <purpose>|not served
  (over 2 MiB|reserve empty|lost) <purpose> <KiB>: held H of N MiB (lowest L),
  served S (KiB), lost, too big, empty, refills, app refused while held A
Purposes: descriptor, upload, query, fence/gs, shader/rings (by priority, domain
and flags as tools/patch-radv-memory-report.py names them).

Unset or 0 (the default): one test of a cached value per buffer, nothing held,
nothing served: as T184. Driver only: no translation id input, no
TranslationSwitches name, no cache key or build id change. KEEPS THE STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_bo.c b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_bo.c
index 9b2ad1d..c55b9d8 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_bo.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_bo.c
@@ -143,11 +143,27 @@ radv_ps5_buffer_create(struct radeon_winsys *rws, uint64_t size, unsigned alignm
    struct radv_ps5_bo *const bo = calloc(1, sizeof(*bo));
    if (!bo)
       return VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY;
+   /* RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_MIB (lead-mesh-46): fills the driver's reserve; one test when unset. */
+   radv_ps5_reserve_tend();
    bool allocated;
    do {
       allocated = replayable ? radv_ps5_memory_alloc_replayable(size, alignment, window32, replay_address, &bo->memory)
                              : radv_ps5_memory_alloc(size, alignment, window32, &bo->memory);
    } while (!allocated && radv_ps5_retired_wait(ws->queue));
+   /* The driver's own buffer the pool refused (not VkDeviceMemory, not captured or replayed) takes a
+    * block of the reserve; the app's device memory does not (lead-mesh-46). */
+   if (!allocated && !replayable) {
+      if (priority > RADV_BO_PRIORITY_APPLICATION_MAX) {
+         const char *const purpose = priority == RADV_BO_PRIORITY_QUERY_POOL ? "query"
+                                     : priority != RADV_BO_PRIORITY_DESCRIPTOR ? "shader/rings"
+                                     : (domain & RADEON_DOMAIN_VRAM) && (flags & RADEON_FLAG_READ_ONLY) ? "descriptor"
+                                     : (flags & RADEON_FLAG_GTT_WC) ? "upload"
+                                                                     : "fence/gs";
+         allocated = radv_ps5_reserve_serve(size, alignment, window32, purpose, &bo->memory);
+      } else {
+         radv_ps5_reserve_note_app_refused(size);
+      }
+   }
    if (!allocated) {
       free(bo);
       return replay_address ? VK_ERROR_INVALID_OPAQUE_CAPTURE_ADDRESS : VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY;
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c
index be2de64..395f48b 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c
@@ -317,6 +317,141 @@ radv_ps5_memory_alloc(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t alignment, bool window32, struct
    return placed;
 }
 
+/* EglantinePS5 RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_MIB=N (lead-mesh-46, off unless set). At the load past
+ * Ocarina's field the pool fills to its last MiB within about 2 s in every start (T184,
+ * the cold-start test at the field), and the app survives a refused image or buffer but not a refused
+ * descriptor pool (vkCreateDescriptorPool, from a draw on the Vulkan worker) or a refused upload
+ * buffer (recorded as the command buffer's error, returned by vkEndCommandBuffer). Both are the
+ * driver's own small buffers, and both are window buffers, which never reach lead-mesh-22's ask.
+ * A limit on the app's allocations alone would not keep the last MiB for them: the guest's memory,
+ * the JIT and the heap take the same pool. So the driver holds the memory itself, as separate
+ * 2 MiB blocks of direct memory (not mapped), and gives one back to the pool and places the
+ * buffer again when the pool refuses an internal buffer of 2 MiB or less. Nothing changes in how
+ * a buffer is placed or freed: a served buffer is an ordinary allocation the kernel made from the
+ * block just released. The reserve is filled at the first buffer and again (at most every 250 ms)
+ * once the largest free piece is at least N + RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_REFILL_MIB (256). */
+#define RADV_PS5_RESERVE_MAX_BLOCKS 256
+static simple_mtx_t radv_ps5_reserve_lock = SIMPLE_MTX_INITIALIZER;
+static int64_t radv_ps5_reserve_block[RADV_PS5_RESERVE_MAX_BLOCKS];
+static uint32_t radv_ps5_reserve_held;     /* blocks, under the lock (read without it as a hint) */
+static int32_t radv_ps5_reserve_target = -1; /* blocks; -1: not read yet */
+static uint64_t radv_ps5_reserve_refill_bytes;
+static int64_t radv_ps5_reserve_tended_ns;
+static uint32_t radv_ps5_reserve_lowest = UINT32_MAX;
+static uint32_t radv_ps5_reserve_served, radv_ps5_reserve_lost, radv_ps5_reserve_big, radv_ps5_reserve_empty;
+static uint32_t radv_ps5_reserve_refills, radv_ps5_reserve_app_refused;
+static uint64_t radv_ps5_reserve_served_bytes;
+
+static uint32_t
+radv_ps5_reserve_target_blocks(void)
+{
+   int32_t target = p_atomic_read(&radv_ps5_reserve_target);
+   if (target >= 0)
+      return (uint32_t)target;
+   const char *const value = getenv("RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_MIB");
+   const unsigned long mib = value ? strtoul(value, NULL, 10) : 0;
+   const char *const refill = getenv("RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_REFILL_MIB");
+   radv_ps5_reserve_refill_bytes = (uint64_t)(refill ? strtoul(refill, NULL, 10) : 256) << 20;
+   target = (int32_t)MIN2((mib + 1) / 2, RADV_PS5_RESERVE_MAX_BLOCKS);
+   p_atomic_set(&radv_ps5_reserve_target, target);
+   return (uint32_t)target;
+}
+
+static void
+radv_ps5_reserve_line(const char *what, const char *purpose, uint64_t bytes)
+{
+   fprintf(stderr,
+           "RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE %s%s%s %llu KiB: held %u of %u MiB (lowest %u), served %u (%llu KiB), "
+           "lost %u, too big %u, empty %u, refills %u, app refused while held %u\n",
+           what, purpose ? " " : "", purpose ? purpose : "", (unsigned long long)(bytes >> 10),
+           radv_ps5_reserve_held * 2, (unsigned)radv_ps5_reserve_target * 2,
+           radv_ps5_reserve_lowest == UINT32_MAX ? radv_ps5_reserve_held * 2 : radv_ps5_reserve_lowest * 2,
+           radv_ps5_reserve_served, (unsigned long long)(radv_ps5_reserve_served_bytes >> 10), radv_ps5_reserve_lost,
+           radv_ps5_reserve_big, radv_ps5_reserve_empty, radv_ps5_reserve_refills,
+           p_atomic_read(&radv_ps5_reserve_app_refused));
+}
+
+void
+radv_ps5_reserve_tend(void)
+{
+   const uint32_t target = radv_ps5_reserve_target_blocks();
+   if (target == 0 || p_atomic_read(&radv_ps5_reserve_held) >= target)
+      return;
+   const int64_t now = os_time_get_nano();
+   const int64_t last = p_atomic_read(&radv_ps5_reserve_tended_ns);
+   if (last != 0 && now - last < INT64_C(250000000))
+      return;
+   if (p_atomic_cmpxchg(&radv_ps5_reserve_tended_ns, last, now) != last)
+      return;
+   const bool first = last == 0;
+   if (!first && radv_ps5_memory_available_bytes() < (uint64_t)target * RADV_PS5_LARGE_BYTES + radv_ps5_reserve_refill_bytes)
+      return;
+   simple_mtx_lock(&radv_ps5_reserve_lock);
+   const uint32_t before = radv_ps5_reserve_held;
+   while (radv_ps5_reserve_held < target) {
+      int64_t physical = -1;
+      if (sceKernelAllocateDirectMemory(0, sceKernelGetDirectMemorySize(), RADV_PS5_LARGE_BYTES, RADV_PS5_LARGE_BYTES,
+                                        RADV_PS5_DIRECT_TYPE, &physical) != 0)
+         break;
+      radv_ps5_reserve_block[radv_ps5_reserve_held++] = physical;
+   }
+   if (radv_ps5_reserve_held > before) {
+      if (!first)
+         radv_ps5_reserve_refills++;
+      if (first || radv_ps5_reserve_refills <= 32)
+         radv_ps5_reserve_line(first ? "on: filled" : "refilled", NULL,
+                               (uint64_t)(radv_ps5_reserve_held - before) * RADV_PS5_LARGE_BYTES);
+   }
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&radv_ps5_reserve_lock);
+}
+
+bool
+radv_ps5_reserve_serve(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t alignment, bool window32, const char *purpose,
+                       struct radv_ps5_memory *out)
+{
+   if (radv_ps5_reserve_target_blocks() == 0)
+      return false;
+   simple_mtx_lock(&radv_ps5_reserve_lock);
+   bool placed = false;
+   const char *what = "served";
+   if (align64(MAX2(bytes, 1), RADV_PS5_PAGE_BYTES) > RADV_PS5_LARGE_BYTES || alignment > RADV_PS5_LARGE_BYTES) {
+      radv_ps5_reserve_big++;
+      what = "not served (over 2 MiB)";
+   } else if (radv_ps5_reserve_held == 0) {
+      radv_ps5_reserve_empty++;
+      what = "not served (reserve empty)";
+   } else {
+      /* At most two blocks per buffer: a block the retry lost went to another thread. */
+      for (unsigned tries = 0; tries < 2 && radv_ps5_reserve_held > 0 && !placed; ++tries) {
+         const int64_t block = radv_ps5_reserve_block[--radv_ps5_reserve_held];
+         sceKernelReleaseDirectMemory(block, RADV_PS5_LARGE_BYTES);
+         placed = radv_ps5_memory_alloc_once(bytes, alignment, window32, out);
+         if (!placed)
+            radv_ps5_reserve_lost++;
+      }
+      radv_ps5_reserve_lowest = MIN2(radv_ps5_reserve_lowest, radv_ps5_reserve_held);
+      if (placed) {
+         radv_ps5_reserve_served++;
+         radv_ps5_reserve_served_bytes += bytes;
+      } else {
+         what = "not served (lost)";
+      }
+   }
+   const uint32_t events = radv_ps5_reserve_served + radv_ps5_reserve_lost + radv_ps5_reserve_big + radv_ps5_reserve_empty;
+   if (events <= 48 || events % 64 == 0)
+      radv_ps5_reserve_line(what, purpose, bytes);
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&radv_ps5_reserve_lock);
+   return placed;
+}
+
+void
+radv_ps5_reserve_note_app_refused(uint64_t bytes)
+{
+   (void)bytes;
+   if (radv_ps5_reserve_target_blocks() != 0 && p_atomic_read(&radv_ps5_reserve_held) > 0)
+      p_atomic_inc(&radv_ps5_reserve_app_refused);
+}
+
 static bool
 radv_ps5_memory_alloc_once(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t alignment, bool window32, struct radv_ps5_memory *out)
 {
@@ -1004,6 +1139,30 @@ radv_ps5_memory_available_bytes(void)
    return radv_ps5_memory_pool_bytes();
 }
 
+/* RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_MIB (lead-mesh-46): the host model never runs out, so nothing is held. */
+void
+radv_ps5_reserve_tend(void)
+{
+}
+
+bool
+radv_ps5_reserve_serve(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t alignment, bool window32, const char *purpose,
+                       struct radv_ps5_memory *out)
+{
+   (void)bytes;
+   (void)alignment;
+   (void)window32;
+   (void)purpose;
+   (void)out;
+   return false;
+}
+
+void
+radv_ps5_reserve_note_app_refused(uint64_t bytes)
+{
+   (void)bytes;
+}
+
 bool
 radv_ps5_memory_alloc(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t alignment, bool window32, struct radv_ps5_memory *out)
 {
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.h b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.h
index 70b718e..960696d 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.h
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.h
@@ -106,6 +106,18 @@ uint64_t radv_ps5_vrange_space_bytes(void);
 uint64_t radv_ps5_memory_pool_bytes(void);
 uint64_t radv_ps5_memory_available_bytes(void);
 
+/* EglantinePS5 RADV_PS5_INTERNAL_RESERVE_MIB=N (lead-mesh-46, off unless set): N MiB of the pool
+ * held by the driver in 2 MiB blocks for its own buffers (descriptor pools, upload buffers, query
+ * pools, fences) of 2 MiB or less, which the app cannot survive being refused. _tend fills the
+ * reserve (at the first buffer, then again once the pool has room); _serve gives up a block to
+ * an internal buffer the pool refused and places it again; _note_app_refused counts the app's
+ * refused device memory while the reserve held. Unset or 0: _tend and _note return after one
+ * test, _serve returns false, nothing is held. */
+void radv_ps5_reserve_tend(void);
+bool radv_ps5_reserve_serve(uint64_t bytes, uint64_t alignment, bool window32, const char *purpose,
+                            struct radv_ps5_memory *out);
+void radv_ps5_reserve_note_app_refused(uint64_t bytes);
+
 /* Writes back and invalidates the CPU cache lines of a range, and orders the
  * evictions before what follows. */
 void radv_ps5_cpu_flush(const void *address, size_t bytes);
